                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names (name of St Mary in <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>,  <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/> and <ref target="#ms_i2"/>;
                           name of Christ in <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i2"/>; name of the Archangel Gabriel in <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>); 
                           numbers and titles of the Psalms, Canticles and Songs; incipits of
                           Canticles and Songs; title of <ref target="#ms_i1.2"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.3"/>; title and incipit of the
                           daily readings of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/>; name, number and traditional interpretation of the Hebrew letters in Psalm 118; word <foreign xml:lang="gez">‘sǝbuḥ’</foreign> in Canticle 10 (written out
                           fully or abbreviated); a few single words in <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>; elements of
                          punctuation marks and text dividers; Ethiopic numerals or their
                           elements; two groups of lines (alternating with black lines) on the opening page of <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/>; three lines (alternating with black lines) on
                           the opening page of <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.5"/>.</seg>
                     </handNote>
