                  <decoDesc>
                     <decoNote type="printedImage" xml:id="d1">
                        <desc>An image of  European origin, inserted between folia 1 and 2, depicting <ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1031VirginAndChild">Virgin and Child</ref>, Salus Populi Romani-type.</desc>
                     </decoNote>
                     <decoNote type="printedImage" xml:id="d2">
                        <desc>An image of European origin, sewn onto folium <locus target="#2v"/>, depicting <ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1005Crucifixion">Crucifixion of Jesus</ref> (the body of Living Jesus is nailed to the cross). 
                           <q xml:lang="gez">በዝስቅለትከ<sic/>፡ ተማህፀንኩ፡ አነ፡ አባ፡ ገበረ፡ ማርያም፡ ከመ፡ ታድህነኒ፡ እምእሳት፡ ብለ<gap reason="illegible" unit="chars" quantity="1"/> ኢየሱስ፡ ናዝራዊ፡ ንጉሠ፡ አይሁድ፡</q> 
                           <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15201GabraMaryam"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Gabra Māryām</persName> appears as the supplicant in the legend. The second part of the legend is a translation of 
                           the Latin inscription placed at the top of the cross, visible on the image: <foreign xml:lang="la">‘Iesus Nazarenus Rex Iudaeorum’</foreign>.
                           The legend is written by the same crude hand as <ref target="#a7"/>, <ref target="#a8"/> and <ref target="#a9"/>. The image is protected by a <term key="protectiveCurtain" ana="#protectiveCurtain">textile curtain</term>.</desc></decoNote>
                     <decoNote type="printedImage" xml:id="d3"> 
                        <desc>An image of European origin, inserted between folia 2 and 3, depicting <term key="deadjesus" ana="#deadjesus">dead Jesus</term> supported by two <term key="angel" ana="#angel">angels</term>.</desc>
                     </decoNote>
                  </decoDesc>
                  
