                           (at least 9 tools were used: <term key="tripleStraightLine" ana="#tripleStraightLine">triple line fillet</term>, <term key="doubleCircle" ana="#doubleCircle">double circle</term>, <term key="corniForm" ana="#corniForm">corni-form</term>, 
                           <term key="XForm" ana="#XForm">x-form</term>, <term key="crissCross" ana="#crissCross">criss-cross</term>, triple dot fillet, interlaced line fillet, double crescent with eye, scored cross hatching
                        </decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b3" type="Sewing">Two pairs of sewing stations.</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b4" type="SewingStations">4</decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b5" type="bindingMaterial">
                           <material key="wood"/>
                           <material key="leather"/>
                        </decoNote>
                        <decoNote xml:id="b6" type="Other">Small holes are visible on the spine fold of the quires close to the head and to the tail of the codex.</decoNote>
